  "worked_solution": "First of all, we need to find the slope of the tangent line at the point $(1,5).$\n\nTo find the slope of the tangent line, we will calculate the derivative using implicit differentiation, assuming that $y=y(x).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(xy) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(5) \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+y & =0 \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-y \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{-y}{x} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{y}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the slope of the tangent at the point $(1,\\,5)$  is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})}_{(1,\\,5)} \\\\  & ={(-\\frac{y}{x})}_{(1,\\,5)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{1} \\\\  & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can write the equation of the tangent at the point $(1,\\,5)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-{y}_{1}) & =m(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ (y-5) & =-5(x-1) \\\\ y & =-5(x-1)+5 \\\\ y & =-5x+10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we just need to find where this tangent line intersects the $y$-axis. At the point $P$ the $x$-coordinate is $0,$ so we set $x=0$ and solve for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-5x+10 \\\\ y & =-5\\cdot 0+10 \\\\ y & =10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of $P$ are $(0,\\,10).$",
